cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Agentic Clinical AI: governed agentic AI for clinical data surveillance and enrollment forecasting"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-31"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/mtariqi/agentic_clinical_ai"
authors:
  - family-names: Islam
    given-names: Md Tariqul
abstract: >-
  A reproducible Snakemake reference pipeline in which two AI agents (clinical
  data surveillance and predictive enrollment intelligence) act on statistical
  findings through a shared governance runtime: least-privilege identities,
  risk-tiered tools gated by autonomy level, a human approval queue, input
  screening, PII redaction, a circuit breaker, a hash-chained audit log, an
  oversight meta-agent and institutional memory of human decisions. Evaluated
  on synthetic multi-country trials with injected ground truth. Not a
  validated GxP system.
keywords:
  - agentic AI
  - clinical trials
  - risk-based quality management
  - central statistical monitoring
  - enrollment forecasting
  - human oversight
  - audit trail
  - ALCOA++
  - prompt injection
  - Snakemake
